# --- Generated / derived outputs (reproducible via run_all.py) ---
# Ignore the derived tree, EXCEPT the presentation figures (the docs embed them
# inline, so they must be committed for the .md to render on GitHub).
# NOTE: to re-include files under an ignored dir, each parent dir must be
# re-included first, hence the stepwise !outputs/ and !outputs/figures/ below.
outputs/*
!outputs/figures/
outputs/figures/*
!outputs/figures/*.png

# --- Exported PDFs (derived from the .md sources via VS Code "Markdown PDF") ---
# The .md files are the source of truth (render on GitHub, diff cleanly).
# PDFs are disposable publishing artifacts -- regenerate on demand, don't commit.
docs/*.pdf
*.pdf

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Session handoff (private, lives in parent dir; ignore if copied in) ---
*_summary.claude

# --- Source data workbooks ---
# The FULL OPUS + CO-OPS workbooks are compiled extracts of publicly-available
# data (NGS OPUS / CO-OPS datums API). We do NOT re-host the full record in this
# public repo -- obtain it from source (see README "Input data") and drop it in
# data/ to run the full study.
# EXCEPTION: the small committed SAMPLE (data/sample/) IS tracked so a fresh clone
# runs out of the box and reproduces the report's worked examples.
#
# Order matters: broad ignores FIRST, then the stepwise sample re-include LAST so
# nothing downstream re-ignores it.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
data/*
!data/sample/
!data/sample/OPUS_sample.xlsx
!data/sample/CO-OPS_sample.xlsx

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
